===Congress===
[[Popular Force]] won in a landslide, taking more than a third of the vote and an absolute majority of 73 out of 130 seats. Behind them in opposition, [[Peruvians for Change]] with 18 seats and [[Broad Front (Peru)|Broad Front]] with 20 seats. Other parties which gained representation in Congress include [[Alliance for the Progress of Peru]] (9 seats), [[Popular Alliance (Peru)|Popular Alliance]] (5 seats) and [[Popular Action (Peru)|Popular Action]] (5 seats).<ref name="IFES Election Guide">{{cite web|url=http://www.electionguide.org/elections/id/2679/|title=ELECTION FOR CONGRESO DE LA REPÚBLICA 2016|access-date=1 June 2016}}</ref>

